#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1023 expect=skipped domain=LB
#note "⚠ RE-CUT 2026-09-08 (R-4.12 hoist): expect moved noViolation -> skipped. `var_exists(TV.VISIT)` was a top-level conjunct, so an absent TV made the whole AND false and the rule reported a SILENT ZERO -- which is what this scenario used to pin. It is now Requirements.Variables.All ["TV.VISIT"], so the rule is gated out and reports SKIPPED naming the variable. Same violations either way; only the status channel moves, which is R-4.11's whole argument. If this EXECUTES again the entry was dropped -- escalate, do not rewrite the pin. PRIOR NOTE: Fix #246 flood arm, KEPT through the D-TA-6a re-authoring: TV is absent entirely, so $tv_visit_keys is the empty set and the vacuous-on-empty membership would be true on every row with a populated (VISIT, VISITNUM). The top-level var_exists(TV.VISIT) guard resolves TV through the dataset resolver, finds nothing, and suppresses the rule with no finding. PMDA-SD1023 gained the same guard at wave TA-4 (CL-G.1 / EC-82 option (a)), completing the Fix #246 family - the twins are byte-identical again."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | ALB | 2  | BASELINE
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 2 | ALB | 99 | WEEK 99
---
